# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 16, report associated text, with
# flag 8. A key that makes text carries the text's code point in a third
# field after an empty modifiers field: a, é and Space. A with Caps Lock
# carries the lock's bit and the text A. The keypad's 1 carries its own
# number, NumLock and the text 1. Enter and Tab make control characters,
# which the text never holds, so they carry no text field. Alt+A makes
# no text, so it carries none. A text event with no key, keysym 0, is
# sent with the key number 0. With flag 2 too, a press and a repeat
# carry the text and a release carries none. Flag 16 without flag 8
# adds no text, and the query still reports it.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report associated text, Text as code points, Event types; ADR-1005 D13 slice 3
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
needs key-events
send "\e[>24u"
key a
key eacute
key space
key A mods=lock
key KP_1 mods=num char="1"
key Return
key Tab
key a mods=alt
cmd key;sym=0;unicode=e5
send "\e[=26u"
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;event=repeat
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;event=release
send "\e[=17u"
key a
key a mods=ctrl
send "\e[?u"
